  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Horace Elgin Dodge was an American automotive pioneer who co-founded Dodge Brothers with his brother John. A gifted machinist, he helped build transmissions and engines for Oldsmobile and Ford before the brothers launched their own automobile marque. His engineering interests also extended to marine engines and fast boats, while his philanthropy supported Detroit’s musical institutions.",
    "html": "<p>Horace Elgin Dodge was an American automotive pioneer who co-founded Dodge Brothers with his brother John. A gifted machinist, he helped build transmissions and engines for Oldsmobile and Ford before the brothers launched their own automobile marque. His engineering interests also extended to marine engines and fast boats, while his philanthropy supported Detroit’s musical institutions.</p>\r\n",
